{
  "note": [
    "Alfie Control East's fabric (DR-106), cut from the one vehicle layout in scripts/fabric-shuttle.mjs -- regenerate from there, do not hand-edit. ALFIE-CONTROL-EAST.metadata.json v2: 2.8 x 3.0 x 4.8, the car's own beam, the eye at the middle. The control panel across the east wall, deck to 1.26, with the slot at the operator's left, the lever at the middle of it and the display at the right; no seat (canon throws the operator forward into the panel, which is a standing station).",
    "East, the 2.45 x 0.9 forward window, sill 1.35: at Kalamontee the bore running 51 m away east with its rails on the bed 1 m below this deck, at Lawanda a concrete buffer 1.8 m off. The bed is the accepted Lawanda berth's, so the rails come into view about 14 m out rather than the 9 m the package estimates from a floor level with this one -- the canon it answers to, rails along the floor of a long tunnel, is met either way.",
    "West, the 1.5 x 2.4 doorway (SHUTTLE-DOOR, open and invisible at a station, a closed leaf while the car moves) and the whole car end-on: benches, the clear freight deck, and off to the right at about 6 m the north doorway with the platform's colder concrete through it. Beyond the car, the west cabin's door and a slot of its window. At Kalamontee alone the line carries on across the platform and finds its west portal, so a 1.2 m slice of the Waiting Area is in sight through it, 19 to 32 m out: its deck, its north wall and its west wall. Its red door and its south wall are well outside that wedge. It is a bare box here; the benches canon furnishes it with are its own room's to place, and this glimpse takes them when that room is cut."
  ],
